        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on promotion scope, target items, and overall objectives.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 128528,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, kicking off our new project: the Seasonal In-Store Food Promotion Corner! We have 21 days to get this live. First step is T1: Define the list of seasonal food items. Let's use this thread to brainstorm ideas for the assortment. I've set up the initial sheet in A1. What kind of products do you think will be a hit?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1",
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "wave",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 433060,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Great start. Given the season, I'd suggest a 'local harvest' theme. We could feature artisanal cheeses, cured meats from regional producers, and maybe some fruit preserves or local honey. This would not only drive sales but also enhance the customer experience by offering something unique.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 439564,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "I like the 'local harvest' idea. It feels premium. We could add some high-quality crackers or artisan bread to complement the cheeses and meats. That would encourage customers to buy multiple items.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 311830,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "That sounds nice. Are we thinking of things people can eat right away, like snacks, or ingredients for cooking?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 433060,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Good question. I think the focus should be on ready-to-eat or easy-to-prepare items for platters and special occasions. It aligns better with a promotional 'corner' feel rather than regular grocery shopping.",
            "mentions": [
              311830
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 128528,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "Agreed. Let's keep it focused on premium, complementary items. I'll start T5 and check with our suppliers on availability for local cheeses and meats. That's a potential risk we need to mitigate early.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 186687,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "what about some cookies or chips",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
